@prefix schema: <https://schema.org/> .
@prefix delphi: <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/> .

sub:Head {
  this: a np:Nanopublication ;
    np:hasAssertion sub:assertion ;
    np:hasProvenance sub:provenance ;
    np:hasPublicationInfo sub:pubinfo .
}

sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/kimura-substitution-rate> a delphi:Concept, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Kernel-checked Lean 4 statement about a model: In a neutral Wright-Fisher population of M gene copies, the rate at which new mutations become fixed equals the mutation rate per copy per generation, whatever M is." ;
    dct:description "In a neutral Wright-Fisher population of M gene copies, the rate at which new mutations become fixed equals the mutation rate per copy per generation, whatever M is." ;
    dct:source "Evolutionary Rate at the Molecular Level (1968)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1038/217624a0> ;
    skos:notation "k = 2N\\mu \\cdot \\frac{1}{2N} = \\mu" ;
    skos:definition """/-- **Kimura (1968).** Under neutral Wright–Fisher evolution, the substitution rate equals the mutation rate, for every population size `M`. -/
theorem neutral_substitution_rate (M : ℕ) (hM : 0 < M) (μ : ℝ) :
    substitutionRate M μ ((wrightFisher M hM).fixationProbability (oneCopy M hM)) = μ"""^^delphi:lean4 ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    delphi:leanDeclaration "Delphi.substitutionRate" ;
    delphi:leanTheorem "Delphi.neutral_substitution_rate", "Delphi.neutral_substitution_rate_diploid", "Delphi.neutral_substitution_rate_tendsto", "Delphi.wrightFisher_fixation_one" ;
    delphi:leanVerified "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    skos:scopeNote "As stated in the module header." ;
    skos:note "The claim as the source states it, which is NOT what the kernel checked: \"Neutral substitution rate equals the mutation rate\" (Evolutionary Rate at the Molecular Level, 1968). What was checked is the statement in dct:description, which is about a model." ;

    rdfs:comment "Status: kernel-checked (Lean 4 accepted the module with zero sorry and standard axioms only). Not expert-validated. Does not establish: anything about organisms. The theorem is exact inside the stated model and silent outside it. The assumptions it rests on, written in the module header and never proved, are: Strict neutrality of the mutations; Constant population size and Wright-Fisher reproduction (non-overlapping generations, multinomial sampling); Independent fates of mutants: the substitution rate is DEFINED, as in Kimura 1968, as (new mutants per generation) x (fixation probability of one mutant). Interference between lineages is excluded by that definition, not proved absent; The mutation rate mu per copy per generation is a free parameter; nothing here measures it. Kernel-checked is not expert-validated: no human expert has validated these statements. Whether the Lean statement faithfully renders the source is a separate assessment record, and so far only one assessor provider has run." ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/4ebb56add61de66744fe8b957ecd7c0bcecc8083/lean/Delphi/Kimura.lean>, <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/lean.json>, <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/kimura-substitution-rate> dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/kimura-substitution-rate> ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/lean-kernel-check-kimura-substitution-rate> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/lean-kernel-check-kimura-substitution-rate> a delphi:EvidenceItem ;
    rdfs:label "Lean 4 kernel accepted Delphi.neutral_substitution_rate with zero sorry and standard axioms; it also rejected 3 deliberately broken variant(s) of this statement or its model" ;
    dct:description "Build receipt. Lean (version 4.35.0, x86_64-w64-windows-gnu, commit eb6cafb7290e8bd5f2937522d8d804f58f02bafc, Release); toolchain leanprover/lean4:v4.35.0; Mathlib v4.35.0 (56a005855ea17e0b0958f73ec801ae140b0a1679). lake build exit 0 in 5.3 s with 0 errors; 0 sorry in lean/Delphi/Kimura.lean (413 lines). #print axioms for Delphi.neutral_substitution_rate, Delphi.neutral_substitution_rate_diploid, Delphi.neutral_substitution_rate_tendsto, Delphi.wrightFisher_fixation_one: Classical.choice, Quot.sound, propext only (Lean's standard axioms; no sorryAx). Mutation evidence (lean/mutate.mjs, 2026-10-31T22:57:06.367Z): 3 deliberate change(s) to this statement or its model were each rejected by the compiler: [kimura-fixation-one-wrong] Statement changed to claim a single copy fixes with probability 1/(M+1) instead of 1/M. Rejected with 2 error(s): Kimura.lean:371:76: error: unsolved goals [kimura-rate-doubled] Statement changed to claim the substitution rate is 2 mu instead of mu. Rejected with 2 error(s): Kimura.lean:386:93: error: unsolved goals [open-problems-certificate-ratio-one] Certificate sabotaged: the ORX-20/C2 elimination is rewritten to claim that a substitution-rate ratio of exactly 1 at equal mutation rates is ruled out. It is not (that is the theorem), so norm_num must fail and the kernel must reject it. Rejected with 1 error(s): EliminationsOpenProblems.lean:17:121: error: Application type mismatch: The argument Controls: 17 of 17 unmodified modules accepted by the same command." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/kimura-substitution-rate> ;
    rdfs:comment "This evidence item establishes that the stated theorem follows from the stated model. Does not establish: anything about organisms. The theorem is exact inside the stated model and silent outside it. The assumptions it rests on, written in the module header and never proved, are: Strict neutrality of the mutations; Constant population size and Wright-Fisher reproduction (non-overlapping generations, multinomial sampling); Independent fates of mutants: the substitution rate is DEFINED, as in Kimura 1968, as (new mutants per generation) x (fixation probability of one mutant). Interference between lineages is excluded by that definition, not proved absent; The mutation rate mu per copy per generation is a free parameter; nothing here measures it. Kernel-checked is not expert-validated: no human expert has validated these statements. Whether the Lean statement faithfully renders the source is a separate assessment record, and so far only one assessor provider has run." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/lean.json>, <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/4ebb56add61de66744fe8b957ecd7c0bcecc8083/lean/mutations.json>, <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/4ebb56add61de66744fe8b957ecd7c0bcecc8083/lean/Delphi/Audit.lean> .
}

